// expat 2.11.0, the version `with get c.expat` pins. Every citation is a line
// of the package's installed header, include/expat.h (or expat_config.h).
//
// XML_Parser (`struct XML_ParserStruct *`) is allocated by XML_ParserCreate or
// XML_ParserCreateNS and freed by XML_ParserFree. The source proof does not
// close XML_ParserCreate on its own because parserCreate stores a back-pointer
// to the parser inside the DTD owned by the same parser (#3124), so the pair
// is stated here.
//
// Raw functions (genuinely unmodeled/unsafe by nature):
// - XML_ParserCreate_MM: takes a custom malloc/realloc/free function-pointer table.
// - XML_SetUserData, XML_SetExternalEntityRefHandlerArg: untyped void* storage
//   with no per-callback type pairing.
// - XML_GetBuffer, XML_GetBuffer64, XML_MemMalloc, XML_MemRealloc, XML_MemFree,
//   XML_FreeContentModel: raw internal buffer / allocator pointers.
// - XML_GetInputContext, XML_GetInputContext64: returns raw pointer + byte
//   offset/size into parser's internal input buffer valid only inside a handler.
// - XML_GetFeatureList: returns a NULL/sentinel-terminated raw array of XML_Feature.
// - XML_ExternalEntityParserCreate: creates a sub-parser linked to a parent parser.
c facts expat:
